Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/20

## Summary

The dwarf multicannon could not be set up. This adds it, in a new module `content/other/dwarf-multicannon`, and Nulodion's "I've lost my cannon." in `dwarven-mine`. Content area from #353. This push replaces the first version with a rewrite checked against the OSRS Wiki, on current `main` (`829b9477d`).

New module `content/other/dwarf-multicannon`, and Nulodion's "I've lost my cannon." in `dwarven-mine`:
- **Set-up** of the base, stand, barrels and furnace, 2, 2, 3 and 3 ticks apart from the click (our timing), on a free 3x3 with the player at the centre. It needs the Dwarf Cannon quest (wiki, Assembly; through `QuestRequirements`, so the default assume-completed mode allows it). The tick after the furnace, it loads up to 30 balls from the inventory ("You load the cannon with 30 cannonballs."; ours, see Caveats). The OSRS varps that client plugins read are set: `dropcannon` stage, `rockthrower` ammo, `ownedmcannon` coord, `mcannon_world` (the world number modulo 128: the varbit is 7 bits, and the client's buff bar script `buff_bar_get_value` compares it with `map_world % 128`), `mcannon_decayed`, and `mcannonmulti` = `1 << 20` while firing (our value, see Caveats).
- **Fire** loads and starts the barrel turning one direction a tick (8 per revolution). Left-click on a firing cannon tops it up (wiki, 20 February 2014). **Load X** (wiki, 24 September 2025: a Load X option adds a custom amount, set in the settings menu; the client's settings script reads it from `option_cannonballs_load_x`): the first use asks "Set load-x cannonballs (1 - 30):" and stores the amount in that varbit with "You will now load N cannonballs when using Load-x.", then loads that many each time. **Empty** (wiki, 8 February 2018): "You unload your cannon and receive Steel cannonball x N.".
- **Targets** (wiki, Targets and Revolutions): each direction has a target region. Straight directions cover the 3-wide column beyond the cannon, diagonals the quadrant beyond its corner. They overlap on the rows and columns one tile off the centre lines, so a monster there is shot twice a revolution: the double-hit tiles RuneLite's Cannon plugin draws. Tiles under the cannon are never shot. A target needs line of sight from the cannon's 3x3. Large monsters are targeted by their south-west tile. In single-way combat, while the owner is under attack, it fires only at the attacker.
- **Hits**: up to 30 damage, 2 Ranged XP per damage dealt (capped at the target's remaining hitpoints, like `PlayerAttackManager`). Accuracy is the owner's own roll for the current weapon and style against the target's heavy ranged defence (wiki, Accuracy): ranged weapons use ranged accuracy; melee and unarmed use melee accuracy for the selected stab/slash/crush; powered staves use the higher of the two. Equipment and prayers count; target-dependent effects (slayer helmet on task and the like) do not.
- **Breaking and decay** (wiki, Breaking/Decay/Death; messages as RuneLite's Timers & Buffs and the Supplies Tracker match them). After 25 minutes set up, the cannon breaks: loc 14916, "<col=ef1020>Your cannon has broken!", and it stops firing. **Repair** gives "You repair your cannon, restoring it to working order." and starts the 25 minutes again. Unrepaired, it disappears 10 minutes later ("Your cannon has decayed. Speak to Nulodion to get a new one!", `mcannon_decayed` = 1). A part-built cannon disappears 35 minutes after set-up.
- **Logout and death**: the cannon stays where it is, and its timers keep running (they are the loc's own despawn timers). On login the owner gets it back. A cannon recorded on the player but missing from the world, after a restart, counts as lost.
- **Nulodion**, "I've lost my cannon." (Transcript:Nulodion):
  - still set up: "Hmmm. I think you'll find it's still happily parked on the spot where you put it." and the rest of that branch;
  - lost, with fewer than 4 free slots: the "free up some inventory space" line;
  - lost: the four parts ("The dwarf gives you a new cannon."). The balls that were in it come back loaded when it is next set up (wiki);
  - otherwise: his "stolen in action" refusal.
- Pick-up (cannon, broken cannon or part-built) returns the parts and balls: "You pick up the cannon. It's really heavy.". The Grand Exchange refuses a cannon with the wiki's message.

New server-only gameval: timer `mcannon_fire`, written as `-1` and assigned by `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py` (65535; timers have no OSRS max). The first version's `mcannon_decay` timer is gone; the break and decay timers are loc durations now.

