## Screenshots / notes for reviewers

Data sources:
- The cache: locs, varps and varbits, and the client's `buff_bar_get_value` script (OpenRune's CS2 bundle 241.1) for `mcannon_world`.
- OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): "Dwarf multicannon" (Assembly; Mechanics: Damage and experience, Accuracy, Revolutions, Targets, Breaking/Decay/Death; Prohibited areas; Changes) and "Transcript:Nulodion".
- RuneLite (BSD): the Cannon, Timers & Buffs and Supplies Tracker plugins, for the message strings they match and the double-hit tiles.

Deviations, guesses and gaps:
- Approximated: the target regions. The wiki only shows them as a picture, so these are the simplest regions that give the wiki's and RuneLite's double-hit tiles. The range of 8 tiles is ours. Line of sight is checked from the cannon's 3x3 to the target's south-west tile.
- Approximated: the single-way rule uses the owner's current attacker (`aggressive_npc` while in combat) and the cannon's own tile for single/multi. In single-way it can still shoot a monster another player is fighting.
- Approximated: powered staves compare ranged accuracy with crush accuracy.
- Guesses (not on the wiki or in the cache): the set-up timing (2, 2, 3, 3 ticks), the automatic load the tick after the furnace and its "You load the cannon with N cannonballs." line (the line's wording matches LostCity's 2004 content scripts, `quests/quest_mcannon/scripts/cannon_setup.rs2`; the timing has no reference, since 2004 set-up was one part per click), `mcannonmulti` = `1 << 20` while firing, the Load X prompt ("Set load-x cannonballs (1 - 30):", asked on first use; OSRS sets the amount in the settings menu, which this change does not add) and its confirmation line, and the Empty line "You unload your cannon and receive Steel cannonball x N.".
- Guesses: "You need to complete the Dwarf Cannon quest before you can set up a cannon." (the real refusal is not on the wiki); "You cannot construct more than one cannon at a time.", "There isn't enough space to set up here." (also LostCity's), "This isn't your cannon!", "Your cannon is already full." (only when it holds 30), "You don't have any ammo to load into the cannon.", "Your cannon is empty.", and the inventory-space lines. Firing stops when the owner logs out. Nulodion gives all four parts even when only part of the cannon was set up.
- Not implemented: granite cannonballs (35 max hit, loaded first); the Combat Achievement capacities (35/45/60); prohibited areas other than the Grand Exchange; bosses destroying cannons, and monsters the cannon can't hit (sand and ammonite crabs, demonic gorillas, kurasks); the 2019 chance of 1 damage instead of 0 at very low accuracy; the ornament kit; the "push" from the south-west tile after loading and walking away; `mcannon_setuptime` and the buff bar's decay timer (`buff_bar_get_value` also reads `%buff_cannon_decay_start`, which is never set, so the client's buff bar shows no decay timer); the player saying "I'm currently under attack" when firing in single-way combat (wiki, Trivia).
- LostCity's 2004 scripts mark some refusal lines as OSRS wording that differs from ours ("This is not your cannon.", "The cannon is already full of ammo.", the pick-up space lines); neither the wiki nor RuneLite settles them, so ours stay as declared guesses.

